WEBVTT

00:00:57.117 --> 00:00:58.243
Fiona and Zeke...

00:00:58.243 --> 00:00:58.952
Kissed.

00:00:58.952 --> 00:01:00.829
Like someone had died.

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:01.579
You're in love.

00:01:01.579 --> 00:01:02.455
Where's your ring?

00:01:02.455 --> 00:01:03.123
Oh no.

00:01:03.498 --> 00:01:04.416
I love her.

00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:07.711
How many times have you tried talking to Aemie?

00:01:09.212 --> 00:01:10.255
I'm sorry, wife.

00:01:10.505 --> 00:01:11.464
I never meant to.

00:01:11.548 --> 00:01:13.258
She initiated the kiss.

00:01:15.969 --> 00:01:16.678
You're staying here.

00:01:16.803 --> 00:01:20.098
Why do you always have to get your way?

00:01:20.265 --> 00:01:21.266
I said I don't want to!

00:01:21.349 --> 00:01:22.350
I said I don't want to!

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:23.351
I said I don't want to!

00:01:23.351 --> 00:01:24.352
I said I don't want to!

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:26.980
I'm pregnant.

00:01:29.065 --> 00:01:30.150
Ouch!

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:31.443
We haven't even...

00:01:31.568 --> 00:01:33.361
The only guy I remember

00:01:33.903 --> 00:01:35.905
Being with recently...

00:01:35.905 --> 00:01:36.990
Was Moo.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:38.241
Fucking asshole!

00:01:38.241 --> 00:01:39.576
I'm gonna kill that bastard!

00:01:42.245 --> 00:01:43.580
Did you know Aemie's pregnant?

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.290
I'll give you 10 minutes to explain.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:46.624
Aemie! Aemie!

00:01:46.624 --> 00:01:48.752
That's impossible, I second the motion!

00:01:48.752 --> 00:01:49.586
Because...

00:01:49.753 --> 00:01:51.045
Moo's gay!

00:01:54.466 --> 00:01:57.010
I'm seriously the only sane one left here.

00:02:03.933 --> 00:02:05.018
Aemie...

00:02:09.189 --> 00:02:10.356
Tomorrow.

00:02:11.274 --> 00:02:12.221
Huh?

00:02:12.525 --> 00:02:13.693
I'll tell you tomorrow.

00:02:15.403 --> 00:02:16.666
For now,

00:02:17.363 --> 00:02:18.281
Get some rest.

00:02:19.115 --> 00:02:20.158
Look at this.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:22.577
Why tomorrow?

00:02:22.577 --> 00:02:24.921
You can tell me now. I'm already here.

00:02:24.946 --> 00:02:26.156
You can do it now.

00:02:26.414 --> 00:02:29.209
Nah, don't get too excited, wife.

00:02:29.751 --> 00:02:33.046
I'm already nervous just thinking about confessing.

00:02:43.681 --> 00:02:44.724
Good night, wife.

00:04:07.056 --> 00:04:08.391
Can you not, Louie Birkins?

00:04:08.391 --> 00:04:10.184
Do you want the sun to never rise for you again?

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.103
Calm down girl, this is Shan.

00:04:14.272 --> 00:04:15.189
Oh, why?

00:04:15.231 --> 00:04:17.066
I just wanna ask something,

00:04:17.066 --> 00:04:18.318
I feel like you could help

00:04:18.985 --> 00:04:21.237
I can't help you with whatever it is that you're asking.

00:04:21.446 --> 00:04:24.949
But this is about Aemie and her husband, Mr. Roswell.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.368
About Cuz and Mr. Roswell?

00:04:27.969 --> 00:04:30.555
Kaizer reached out to me asking for help.

00:04:32.206 --> 00:04:35.168
You know what? Maybe we should just talk about it at school.

00:04:35.168 --> 00:04:36.336
This will be quick

00:04:36.586 --> 00:04:38.838
Later. You're going to school anyway, right?

00:04:39.464 --> 00:04:41.799
- Alright, bye, see you. - Okay, bye.

00:04:46.304 --> 00:04:47.347
Good morning, Momo.

00:04:47.513 --> 00:04:48.556
Good morning, Auntie.

00:04:49.891 --> 00:04:51.684
Ugh, it's still early!

00:04:51.851 --> 00:04:53.394
What are you doing at our house?

00:04:53.394 --> 00:04:55.188
Well, of course. I'm here to pick up my Momo.

00:04:55.188 --> 00:04:56.314
Come on, let's go together.

00:04:56.481 --> 00:04:56.981
Huh?

00:04:57.565 --> 00:04:58.691
Oh, dear.

00:04:58.775 --> 00:05:00.944
Niece, you're so noisy this early in the morning.

00:05:00.944 --> 00:05:01.861
Go eat.

00:05:02.278 --> 00:05:04.697
Oh, Louie, just help yourself.

00:05:05.114 --> 00:05:05.823
Yes, Auntie.

00:05:05.907 --> 00:05:08.159
I know your cooking is always delicious.

00:05:08.618 --> 00:05:09.619
Hmm, really?

00:05:09.827 --> 00:05:11.537
Well then, keep eating, okay?

00:05:11.829 --> 00:05:14.248
I'm just preparing the food I'm selling later.

00:05:14.248 --> 00:05:15.917
You know, Auntie, if I didn't have class,

00:05:15.917 --> 00:05:17.627
I'd even help you sell.

00:05:18.211 --> 00:05:18.900
Ass-kisser.

00:05:19.879 --> 00:05:23.091
There's no such thing as excuses when someone truly wants to help.

00:05:23.091 --> 00:05:24.384
Exactly.

00:05:24.717 --> 00:05:25.635
Here.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:29.389
Louie, sell my sticky rice cake to your classmates.

00:05:29.722 --> 00:05:31.516
Twenty-five pesos per slice.

00:05:31.808 --> 00:05:33.518
But we have a promo, okay?

00:05:33.726 --> 00:05:35.812
Fifty pesos, buy one, take one.

00:05:36.771 --> 00:05:37.804
Huh?

00:05:39.357 --> 00:05:42.527
Auntie, are you really making me sell sticky rice cake?

00:05:43.569 --> 00:05:45.363
Why are you complaining?

00:05:45.613 --> 00:05:47.240
Auntie, I don't think he wants to.

00:05:47.532 --> 00:05:48.366
He's complaining.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:50.702
No, no, no, Momo.

00:05:51.035 --> 00:05:52.036
Auntie, I don't think this is enough.

00:05:52.036 --> 00:05:53.037
Maybe you have more back there.

00:05:53.538 --> 00:05:54.288
Really?

00:05:54.288 --> 00:05:54.789
Then,

00:05:54.789 --> 00:05:56.290
Sell my <i>tapsilog</i>,

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.750
My <i>longsilog</i>, and my<i> hotsilog</i>.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.544
Don't worry, they're packed in Styrofoam.

00:05:59.752 --> 00:06:00.962
They won't be hard to carry.

00:06:01.129 --> 00:06:01.963
Okay, Auntie.

00:06:01.963 --> 00:06:02.422
That's fine.

00:06:02.422 --> 00:06:04.674
Momo's coming with me to sell them anyway, right?

00:06:05.133 --> 00:06:05.959
Oh no.

00:06:06.509 --> 00:06:08.636
Come on, we're gonna be late.

00:06:08.636 --> 00:06:10.722
Auntie, we're heading out.

00:06:11.055 --> 00:06:12.265
I'm gonna be late.

00:06:12.265 --> 00:06:13.933
There goes my niece.

00:06:14.475 --> 00:06:15.852
Take care, okay?

00:06:15.852 --> 00:06:17.687
Louie, take good care of my niece, okay?

00:06:17.687 --> 00:06:18.604
Yes, Auntie.

00:06:18.604 --> 00:06:20.690
I'll take good care of your most beautiful niece.

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:21.482
- Most beautiful? - Let's go.

00:06:21.482 --> 00:06:24.027
I'm her only niece, obviously.

00:06:24.027 --> 00:06:25.570
Move. You go first.

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:26.529
Bye!

00:06:26.529 --> 00:06:27.780
- Bye, Auntie! - Bye, Auntie!

00:06:40.835 --> 00:06:41.711
Yeah.

00:06:42.545 --> 00:06:44.255
The boss already knows about Yaji.

00:06:44.589 --> 00:06:46.632
But I didn't tell him about your dad.

00:06:46.883 --> 00:06:49.469
If I tell him, then surely even you...

00:06:49.969 --> 00:06:50.511
What?

00:06:51.095 --> 00:06:52.680
Aemie's husband will kill me too?

00:06:53.014 --> 00:06:54.599
Yeah, definitely.

00:06:56.809 --> 00:06:58.519
But Aemie's my friend.

00:06:58.519 --> 00:06:59.020
And...

00:06:59.353 --> 00:07:02.148
I'm sure she wouldn't do that to Aemie's friend, right?

00:07:02.482 --> 00:07:04.609
Mr. Roswell...

00:07:04.609 --> 00:07:06.486
Killed Kaizer's parents,

00:07:06.486 --> 00:07:07.445
Jerson's parents,

00:07:07.445 --> 00:07:08.780
And Wallace's parents.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:08.988
Those three are her friends, right?

00:07:08.988 --> 00:07:10.990
Those three are his friends.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:13.076
And you're just his wife's friend.

00:07:13.076 --> 00:07:13.993
But, Vash.

00:07:14.744 --> 00:07:17.288
What if they find out Aemie is Dad's real daughter?

00:07:17.914 --> 00:07:19.791
How can we stop them from killing each other?

00:07:20.708 --> 00:07:21.292
No.

00:07:21.292 --> 00:07:23.836
It's safer if no one finds out.

00:07:27.465 --> 00:07:28.758
But, what about Auntie Yana?

00:07:29.842 --> 00:07:30.510
I mean,

00:07:31.344 --> 00:07:33.262
I wanna know more about what happened to her.

00:07:33.763 --> 00:07:36.474
Why does it feel like she doesn't know anything about what's happening?

00:07:37.183 --> 00:07:39.393
Cai, let's just stay out of it.

00:07:39.393 --> 00:07:40.978
You might end up getting hurt.

00:07:41.437 --> 00:07:44.899
Alright. I have to go. Call you later.

00:08:14.095 --> 00:08:16.097
No, you can't do this!

00:08:16.097 --> 00:08:17.515
Alyana, I have to do this!

00:08:17.515 --> 00:08:18.641
No!

00:08:22.687 --> 00:08:23.688
I am...

00:08:26.858 --> 00:08:28.901
Alyana Heartily-Ferrer.

00:08:34.323 --> 00:08:36.117
I finally remembered my name.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:41.164
But I still don't understand.

00:08:44.917 --> 00:08:47.170
Why is my last name Ferrer when...

00:08:48.045 --> 00:08:49.589
Miguel is my husband?

00:08:50.298 --> 00:08:51.716
That's why I love you, babe.

00:08:52.091 --> 00:08:53.092
I know, right?

00:08:58.681 --> 00:08:59.682
Unless...

00:09:00.975 --> 00:09:02.727
He's not really my husband.

00:09:03.895 --> 00:09:05.605
Or maybe I'm a cheater?

00:09:07.064 --> 00:09:10.943
Who is that man I keep seeing whenever my head starts to hurt?

00:09:13.779 --> 00:09:14.572
And...

00:09:16.699 --> 00:09:18.618
Why do I seem so rich?

00:09:19.744 --> 00:09:21.245
And why are there so many shootouts?

00:09:37.094 --> 00:09:40.181
I feel like the villain in an action movie!

00:09:41.933 --> 00:09:42.945
Who?

00:09:43.768 --> 00:09:45.811
Who is that girl I see?

00:09:46.854 --> 00:09:48.397
Staring straight

00:09:49.106 --> 00:09:50.358
Back at me.

00:09:51.484 --> 00:09:52.944
I need to find out

00:09:53.444 --> 00:09:55.446
Who I really am as

00:09:55.446 --> 00:09:57.448
Alyana Heartily-Ferrer.

00:09:58.032 --> 00:10:01.035
Before I tell Baby Ae and my niece.

00:10:25.935 --> 00:10:27.024
Hi!

00:10:27.561 --> 00:10:28.938
You're Aemie, right?

00:10:31.023 --> 00:10:32.024
Can I sit here?

00:10:32.316 --> 00:10:33.276
Oh, sure.

00:10:35.069 --> 00:10:36.079
Wow.

00:10:37.154 --> 00:10:38.281
You know me?

00:10:41.367 --> 00:10:42.345
Mmm.

00:10:43.327 --> 00:10:44.453
You're...

00:10:45.538 --> 00:10:46.563
Me?

00:10:47.707 --> 00:10:48.749
I'm your...

00:10:49.875 --> 00:10:51.001
Guardian angel.

00:10:53.879 --> 00:10:55.006
Oh my!

00:10:56.048 --> 00:10:57.423
You're an angel?!

00:10:58.217 --> 00:10:59.927
No wonder you're so beautiful.

00:11:01.887 --> 00:11:03.764
Why did you come down to Earth?

00:11:05.182 --> 00:11:06.767
Can I see your wings?

00:11:07.435 --> 00:11:08.561
Where are your wings?

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:13.941
Can we be friends?

00:11:14.984 --> 00:11:16.360
Of course! Seriously!

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:19.196
Why would I say no to being friends with a real angel?

00:11:20.656 --> 00:11:24.702
I'm not literally an angel, but I'm your guardian angel—

00:11:24.702 --> 00:11:25.691
Ma'am Aemie!

00:11:26.454 --> 00:11:27.872
Jacob, come here, quick!

00:11:28.331 --> 00:11:29.105
Hurry!

00:11:32.626 --> 00:11:33.636
Oh no!

00:11:34.045 --> 00:11:35.066
Huh?

00:11:35.129 --> 00:11:36.213
Where did she go?

00:11:36.922 --> 00:11:38.035
The angel?

00:11:40.968 --> 00:11:41.802
Where'd she go?

00:11:41.802 --> 00:11:43.637
Ma'am, who was that?

00:11:44.764 --> 00:11:47.224
Oh, that was my guardian angel.

00:11:49.852 --> 00:11:50.603
Why are you here?

00:11:51.854 --> 00:11:53.107
Are you here to get a free meal from me?

00:11:53.898 --> 00:11:56.400
Oh, you just missed Louie earlier!

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.027
There was so much sticky rice cake!

00:12:04.533 --> 00:12:05.451
Hey, Jacob!

00:12:06.786 --> 00:12:07.553
Hey!

00:12:07.578 --> 00:12:08.371
Oh, sorry, ma'am.

00:12:08.371 --> 00:12:09.538
Oh, it's Mr. Roswell.

00:12:10.206 --> 00:12:11.374
He wants to talk to you.

00:12:14.168 --> 00:12:15.086
Hi, Dong.

00:12:15.086 --> 00:12:17.338
What on earth have you been up to?

00:12:18.631 --> 00:12:20.091
Oh no!

00:12:20.549 --> 00:12:21.092
Oh, sorry!

00:12:21.092 --> 00:12:23.552
I forgot to charge my phone again.

00:12:23.719 --> 00:12:25.179
Get ready later.

00:12:25.179 --> 00:12:26.806
No. Just listen first.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:31.435
That's not fair!

00:12:31.936 --> 00:12:33.646
Why not just tell me now?

00:12:35.231 --> 00:12:38.109
Yesterday you said tomorrow, and today is already "tomorrow."

00:12:38.109 --> 00:12:39.630
I'll be the one to fetch you later.

00:12:39.693 --> 00:12:41.622
So meet me at the gate. We'll go somewhere.

00:12:41.647 --> 00:12:42.988
Really? Okay, okay.

00:12:42.988 --> 00:12:43.989
Alright, alright, alright.

00:12:44.949 --> 00:12:45.866
Aye, aye, Captain!

00:12:48.327 --> 00:12:49.120
Bye-bye, bye-bye.

00:12:50.788 --> 00:12:51.789
Oh, Jacob, your phone.

00:12:55.334 --> 00:12:56.460
Hey, Jacob, your phone!

00:12:56.669 --> 00:12:57.503
Oh, sorry, ma'am.

00:12:57.503 --> 00:12:58.212
Thank you.

00:12:59.505 --> 00:13:01.757
Ma'am, wasn't that girl pretty?

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:18.315
Here's the entire map of the Grand Park Hotel.

00:13:20.067 --> 00:13:22.736
Your target is the hotel owner.

00:13:24.697 --> 00:13:25.865
Alexander Park.

00:13:27.158 --> 00:13:30.744
There will be a big transaction at around 9 in the evening.

00:13:31.412 --> 00:13:34.248
So, we only have a few hours left to prepare.

00:13:35.249 --> 00:13:38.043
Do we need a negotiator for that transaction?

00:13:38.043 --> 00:13:39.081
No.

00:13:39.962 --> 00:13:42.173
He's going to meet someone, and we don't care.

00:13:42.798 --> 00:13:45.426
Our aim is Young here.

00:13:46.135 --> 00:13:48.137
Finish off his target.

00:13:48.804 --> 00:13:49.847
Nothing else.

00:13:50.264 --> 00:13:51.974
Do we really need to go with Young?

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:54.727
Just so he can take out his target?

00:13:55.352 --> 00:13:56.534
I mean,

00:13:57.188 --> 00:13:58.230
This guy is old enough.

00:13:59.023 --> 00:14:00.136
He can handle it.

00:14:00.566 --> 00:14:03.152
Don't underestimate Alexander Park.

00:14:03.277 --> 00:14:04.737
According to my sources,

00:14:05.196 --> 00:14:06.947
There'll be a lot of guards at the location later.

00:14:07.072 --> 00:14:08.282
The more, the merrier.

00:14:09.742 --> 00:14:12.036
Our directive is to shoot on sight.

00:14:12.453 --> 00:14:15.748
Anyone who tries to interfere with our mission gets a bullet to the head.

00:14:16.749 --> 00:14:17.923
And you, Young...

00:14:19.793 --> 00:14:21.504
You will focus on your target.

00:14:24.215 --> 00:14:25.257
Any questions?

00:14:26.634 --> 00:14:27.510
Nah.

00:14:27.968 --> 00:14:29.261
I'm good.

00:14:29.261 --> 00:14:29.970
Okay.

00:14:30.888 --> 00:14:31.388
Good.

00:14:31.847 --> 00:14:32.765
Let's get ready.

00:14:33.557 --> 00:14:36.644
We need to be there as early as possible to survey the area.

00:14:44.485 --> 00:14:47.404
And remember, keep your guard up.

00:14:48.113 --> 00:14:49.990
We don't know who's going to be there until we get there.

00:14:56.247 --> 00:14:57.373
Shit!

00:14:59.041 --> 00:14:59.792
Are you ready?

00:15:00.751 --> 00:15:01.877
Are you ready?

00:15:02.461 --> 00:15:03.504
How about you, babe? Are you ready?

00:15:03.504 --> 00:15:04.630
I'm so ready.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:05.464
Let's do this.

00:15:05.589 --> 00:15:06.257
You're ready?

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:08.715
Let's go.

00:15:15.432 --> 00:15:16.892
Grand Park Hotel.

00:15:20.896 --> 00:15:22.231
This place is huge, huh?

00:15:23.566 --> 00:15:25.943
Are you sure the meeting with Park is still happening tonight?

00:15:27.403 --> 00:15:28.112
Of course.

00:15:28.862 --> 00:15:30.114
He's meeting with the boss.

00:15:30.906 --> 00:15:34.785
Once we're there, he won't have any choice but to talk to the boss.

00:15:35.494 --> 00:15:36.036
If...

00:15:36.745 --> 00:15:38.122
All they're gonna do is talk.

00:15:39.373 --> 00:15:40.708
I hope not.

00:15:41.834 --> 00:15:43.178
That's the part I'm looking forward to.

00:15:43.669 --> 00:15:44.913
The...

00:15:45.588 --> 00:15:46.505
Action.

00:15:52.511 --> 00:15:54.221
Well, look who's finally here.

00:15:55.681 --> 00:15:57.186
Why are you always off on your own?

00:15:57.224 --> 00:15:59.101
Our starting five is never complete because of you.

00:15:59.268 --> 00:16:00.227
I've just been busy.

00:16:00.227 --> 00:16:01.327
Busy?

00:16:02.021 --> 00:16:03.731
We're all in the same group.

00:16:04.413 --> 00:16:05.374
How come

00:16:05.399 --> 00:16:06.506
We're not that busy?

00:16:07.568 --> 00:16:09.897
Just make sure you're not hiding anything.

00:16:14.241 --> 00:16:15.534
So what's happening tonight?

00:16:20.164 --> 00:16:22.166
Alexander Park, 43 years old.

00:16:22.333 --> 00:16:24.960
A businessman, and an arms dealer.

00:16:25.294 --> 00:16:27.338
He's smuggling the latest firearm models.

00:16:28.505 --> 00:16:30.132
Arms dealing is Roswell territory.

00:16:30.841 --> 00:16:31.800
Exactly.

00:16:32.801 --> 00:16:34.928
That's why Mr. Roswell is meeting with him.

00:16:36.013 --> 00:16:37.514
He's going to negotiate,

00:16:37.514 --> 00:16:38.932
And if he refuses to cooperate...

00:16:40.434 --> 00:16:40.976
Boom.

00:16:43.937 --> 00:16:46.148
But did I hear that right? Ma'am Aemie is coming too?

00:16:48.776 --> 00:16:49.693
That's what the boss said.

00:16:50.736 --> 00:16:51.689
Why?

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:17.988
Hello?

00:17:18.013 --> 00:17:18.597
Dong?

00:17:18.681 --> 00:17:19.823
Where are you?

